# ==== T-FMT-C · inline suite x header TRAILING COMMENT
#
# AXIS (6 cells): {match case, if, elif, else, on error, meta case} each
#   spelled inline WITH a trailing comment on the header line. The comment
#   must land AFTER the inline statement and the output must REPARSE.
#
# THE MECHANISM IS **DEFER**, NOT SUPPRESS. A header's trailing-comment hook
# naturally fires right after the `:`; on an inline suite that puts the
# comment BEFORE the statement, so the statement ends up INSIDE the comment
# and the file no longer parses. Suppressing the hook instead is wrong at the
# match-arm site: an inline arm body is an EXPRESSION, so no statement-side
# hook exists to claim the comment and it would leak to the NEXT arm as a
# bogus leading line. Deferring is provably safe — the comment cursor is
# monotone (no double-emit) and `emit_remaining_comments` catches any straggler
# (no drop).
#
# RED pre-fix (recorded 2026-08-11) — the match-arm cell was a LIVE
# non-reparsing defect, independent of this track's layout work:
#     `case 1: 10  # one`  -->  `case 1:  # one 10`
#   and `gg parse` on that output failed with 10 errors
#   (`expected INDENT, found 'else'`). The other five cells were latent: their
#   suites always exploded, which hid the same pre-wired ordering.
#
# ⚠ CHOSEN BEHAVIOUR for a MULTI-LINE inline child (`if true: int x = match y:`
#   with a header comment): DEFER lands the comment after the child's LAST
#   line. It reparses and no comment is lost, but the comment MOVES. That cell
#   lives in `inline_multiline_child_comment.gg`.

int arm_comment(int x):
    int r = match x:
        case 1: 10  # one
        else: 20  # other
    return r

void if_comment(int x):
    if x == 1: print(1)  # then
    elif x == 2: print(2)  # otherwise
    else: print(3)  # fallback

void on_error_comment():
    on error print(9)  # recover

String meta_case_comment[T]():
    meta match typename(T):
        case "int": return "i"  # ints
        else: return "o"  # rest

void main():
    print(arm_comment(1))
    if_comment(1)
    on_error_comment()
    print(meta_case_comment[int]())
